# Cost Tracking Guidelines

Helicone tracks token costs for all supported LLM providers. This document outlines the conventions and patterns for adding or updating cost data.

## Directory Structure

```
costs/
  src/
    providers/
      openai/
        index.ts        # Model cost definitions
      anthropic/
        index.ts
      google/
        index.ts
      ... (other providers)
    interface.ts        # Shared types and interfaces
    index.ts            # Aggregated exports
```

## Cost Entry Format

Each model cost entry must conform to the `ModelRow` interface:

```typescript
interface ModelRow {
  model: {
    operator: "equals" | "startsWith" | "includes";
    value: string;
  };
  cost: {
    prompt_token: number;   // Cost per prompt token in USD
    completion_token: number; // Cost per completion token in USD
  };
}
```

## Adding a New Model Cost

1. Locate the appropriate provider file under `costs/src/providers/<provider>/index.ts`
2. Add a new entry to the provider's cost array
3. Use the most specific `operator` possible (`equals` > `startsWith` > `includes`)
4. Costs must be expressed in **USD per single token** (not per 1K tokens)

### Conversion Example

If a provider lists pricing as `$3.00 / 1M tokens`:

```typescript
// $3.00 / 1,000,000 = 0.000003 per token
const prompt_token = 3.0 / 1_000_000; // 0.000003
```

## Operator Selection Rules

| Scenario | Operator |
|---|---|
| Exact model name known (e.g., `gpt-4o`) | `equals` |
| Model family with versioned suffixes (e.g., `gpt-4-turbo-*`) | `startsWith` |
| Model name appears anywhere in identifier | `includes` |

## Provider Registration

After adding a provider file, register it in `costs/src/index.ts`:

```typescript
import { costs as openAICosts } from "./providers/openai";
import { costs as myNewProviderCosts } from "./providers/my-new-provider";

export const costs: ModelRow[] = [
  ...openAICosts,
  ...myNewProviderCosts,
  // order matters — more specific entries should come first
];
```

## Testing Cost Entries

- Run `cd costs && npm test` to validate all cost entries
- Ensure no duplicate model entries exist for the same provider
- Verify costs are non-negative and non-zero
- Cross-check against the provider's official pricing page before submitting

## Common Mistakes

- ❌ Using per-1K token pricing directly (must divide by 1000)
- ❌ Using per-1M token pricing directly (must divide by 1,000,000)
- ❌ Forgetting to export the new provider in the root `index.ts`
- ❌ Using `includes` when `equals` or `startsWith` is more appropriate
- ❌ Adding costs without a source URL in the PR description

## PR Checklist for Cost Updates

- [ ] Costs sourced from official provider pricing page (include URL in PR)
- [ ] Correct operator used for model matching
- [ ] Per-token conversion verified
- [ ] No duplicate entries
- [ ] Tests pass locally
- [ ] Provider registered in root `index.ts` (if new provider)
